{
  "summary": "Stores multipath relationship metadata in the wallet for both imported and automatically generated descriptors. Updates WalletDescriptor to track the sibling ScriptPubKeyMan IDs produced from an expansion, enabling the wallet to reconstruct original multipath descriptors. Exposes the reconstructed string via listdescriptors and updates exportwatchonly to retain this association.",
  "problem": "When multipath descriptors are imported into a wallet, they are expanded and stored as independent descriptors without preserving their relationship. Users coordinating with hardware signers that require policy registration cannot retrieve or re-verify the original multipath descriptor through RPC.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'This is useful for working with hardware wallets that require policy registration, particularly those that require resending the descriptor that was registered.'"
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [
      "#36442",
      "#36443"
    ],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "Stacked on top of #36442 (multipath descriptor representation) and #36443 (multipath descriptor reconstruction), which account for the initial commits in the branch. Touches wallet serialization, RPC outputs, and key derivation utilities.",
  "changed_since_previous": "",
  "card": "This pull request stores multipath descriptor relationships in the wallet database and exposes the reconstructed multipath descriptor in listdescriptors and watch-only exports. Currently, Bitcoin Core expands multipath descriptors on import and discards the link between expanded paths, making it impossible to retrieve the registered multipath descriptor needed by certain hardware wallet policies. By storing relative ScriptPubKeyMan IDs in WalletDescriptor, the wallet can reconstruct the original multipath strings. The PR depends on #36442 and #36443 for descriptor representation and reconstruction.",
  "needs": [
    "diff"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium",
  "uncertainties": [
    "The full patch diff was not provided, though the commit log and PR description detail the architecture."
  ],
  "risk": {
    "level": "high",
    "touches": [
      "wallet",
      "wallet_storage",
      "rpc_api"
    ],
    "why": "Modifications to wallet descriptor storage and derivation reconstruction could cause wallet database corruption, loss of access to keys, or incorrect addresses generated for signing."
  }
}
